+/**
+ * Process-wide singleton "owner" wrapper around pimRegEditLoop, the install
+ * step that applies/rolls back Windows registry changes declared in product
+ * XML. One of 7 near-identical Loop-owner wrapper singletons in pim_core.
+ *
+ * Locking contract: TryLock()-gated on an internal mutex, held for the full
+ * duration of the operation -- same pattern as pimCopier/pimShortcuts/
+ * pimServices/pimDownloader.
+ *
+ * CONFIRMED COMMENT/BEHAVIOR MISMATCH: Create()/Uninstall() below are
+ * commented as "these WAIT until they are able to start ... and then they
+ * return immediately," but the actual implementation is a non-blocking
+ * TryLock() that returns false immediately if busy -- identical in shape to
+ * every other wrapper's TryLock-gated methods. The confirmed caller
+ * (pimEntitlement::ApplyRegistryChanges()) explicitly busy-polls with a
+ * sleep on a false return, which would be unnecessary if this method
+ * actually blocked. Trust the implementation and the call-site usage, not
+ * this comment.
+ *
+ * Confirmed gap (shared with pimShortcuts/pimServices/pimDownloader):
+ * Cancel() only sets a flag; the owned pimRegEditLoop is not stopped by it.
+ *
+ * Sole caller in this codebase: pimEntitlement.
+ */
 class pimRegEdit
 {
 private:
